{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1641","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Two Arrays"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Sam changed his school and on the first biology lesson he got a very interesting task about genes."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$n$$$ arrays, the $$$i$$$-th of them contains $$$m$$$ different integers — $$$a_{i,1}, a_{i,2},\\ldots,a_{i,m}$$$. Also you are given an array of integers $$$w$$$ of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find the minimum value of $$$w_i + w_j$$$ among all pairs of integers $$$(i, j)$$$ ($$$1 \\le i, j \\le n$$$), such that the numbers $$$a_{i,1}, a_{i,2},\\ldots,a_{i,m}, a_{j,1}, a_{j,2},\\ldots,a_{j,m}$$$ are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le 5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The $$$i$$$-th of the next $$$n$$$ lines starts with $$$m$$$ distinct integers $$$a_{i,1}, a_{i,2}, \\ldots, a_{i,m}$$$ and then $$$w_i$$$ follows ($$$1\\leq a_{i,j} \\leq 10^9$$$, $$$1 \\leq w_{i} \\leq 10^9$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print a single number — the answer to the problem. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are no suitable pairs $$$(i, j)$$$, print $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 2\n1 2 5\n4 3 1\n2 3 2\n4 5 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 3\n1 2 3 5\n2 3 4 2\n3 4 5 3\n1 3 10 10\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test the minimum value is $$$5 = w_3 + w_4$$$, because numbers $$$\\{2, 3, 4, 5\\}$$$ are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, there are no suitable pair $$$(i, j)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1641D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1641/problem/D"}